#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100662 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "0713e68d-2b3e-5010-954f-7891d96bdbbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3640" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $h(x)$ | $z(x)$ | $h'(x)$ | $z'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $-4$ | $2$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right)$ at $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right) = \\dfrac{h'(x)z(x)-h(x)z'(x)}{(z(x))^2}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{h(x)}{z(x)})|}_{x=-1} & =\\frac{{h}^{′}(-1)z(-1)-h(-1){z}^{′}(-1)}{(z(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot 3}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "787e9681-8009-5ba8-acda-6d8830397d18" :question/math-academy-id "e-3641" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ we have\n\n$$\nf(1)=2, \\quad f'(1)=2, \\quad g(1)=-1, \\quad g'(1)=3.\n$$\n\nIf  $h(x) = \\left( f(x)-1 \\right)\\left(2g(x)+1\\right),$  compute  $h'(1).$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big(uv\\Big) = u \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} +v \\dfrac{\\textrm du}{\\textrm d x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=f(x)-1$ and $v=2g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = f'(x) \\qquad  \\text{and}\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} = 2g'(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(f(x)-1)\\cdot 2{g}^{′}(x)+(2g(x)+1)\\cdot {f}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2{g}^{′}(x)(f(x)-1)+{f}^{′}(x)(2g(x)+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(1) & =2{g}^{′}(1)(f(1)-1)+{f}^{′}(1)(2g(1)+1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot (2-1)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot (-1)+1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100749 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "a87386d5-4a1b-539c-aeb9-dd60181baa4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6154" :question/problem "The values of functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $p(x)$ | $q(x)$ | $p'(x)$ | $q'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big( p(x) + 5q(x) \\big)$ at $x=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( p(x) + 5q(x) \\right) = p'(x) + 5q'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(p(x)+5q(x))|}_{x=-3} & ={p}^{′}(-3)+5{q}^{′}(-3) \\\\  & =0+5\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100750 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "d1d0a3ec-2a84-580a-968e-53b773510853" :question/math-academy-id "e-6155" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big)$ at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big) = f(x)g'(x)+f'(x)g(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & =f(0){g}^{′}(0)+{f}^{′}(0)g(0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "156c59f0-8805-5320-96bd-a85c8169635d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572847} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d0941b-925c-5642-a0ab-3f758fe54938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573055} {:answer/id #uuid "ced4a5a5-5518-548c-8149-4b9efe5bb842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573085} {:answer/id #uuid "de589cad-fcd0-5952-b5df-b25f56c879b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573109} {:answer/id #uuid "e778a5a5-8646-5547-a246-55b51b7bda90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e778a5a5-8646-5547-a246-55b51b7bda90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573121} :answer-field/id #uuid "51e1d4e6-54b3-55d6-bdbd-d6b17b3f1c60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f8b5f6f-ca62-5fd3-b5bd-ae649230f08c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104443" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(0)=5,\\,{f}^{′}(0)=-2,\\,g(0)=10,\\,{g}^{′}(0)=4\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & =f(0){g}^{′}(0)+g(0){f}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4+10\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff58db8-d3aa-5a86-9a2e-d31f49b75188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572899} {:answer/id #uuid "68492c09-b3b0-534b-b4ac-c01f2c0700c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572950} {:answer/id #uuid "81d458d2-90b1-5a94-9db8-718b9d6a3cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572990} {:answer/id #uuid "8801afb1-04ef-5a19-83e4-2ad30cea2606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572998} {:answer/id #uuid "e2372e0b-2f40-5aea-92e5-d19c0b4ba47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5e}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8801afb1-04ef-5a19-83e4-2ad30cea2606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572998} :answer-field/id #uuid "b80dda05-df9e-5706-9ab3-92f41f323fc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65401c01-5232-5bed-88ce-91552174b310" :question/math-academy-id "q-104450" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-4)=2e,\\,{f}^{′}(-4)=-e,\\,g(-4)=-3e,\\,{g}^{′}(-4)=e\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=-4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-4} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(-4)g(-4)-f(-4){g}^{′}(-4)}{{g}^{2}(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-e\\cdot (-3e)-2e\\cdot e}{9{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b976180-84b8-58a3-a43a-9172cb5e18cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572836} {:answer/id #uuid "82a4e697-d4bd-5169-a570-30a241986662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572992} {:answer/id #uuid "8f52e008-4f26-5045-a87f-360235315a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573009} {:answer/id #uuid "de0cafdb-0154-5d5d-893a-c1482d672b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573108} {:answer/id #uuid "e543b8bb-072a-5db3-8955-6993036a65f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82a4e697-d4bd-5169-a570-30a241986662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572992} :answer-field/id #uuid "46a62989-ea6e-5fa9-8951-dcdfb50d24ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e56f348b-304a-594f-855c-44aa9e7abb11" :question/math-academy-id "q-16096" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $-2$ | $-7$ | $1$ | $10$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=-4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-4$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=-4} & =f(-4){g}^{′}(-4)+g(-4){f}^{′}(-4) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 10+(-7)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5026daa1-5493-55d5-b06a-ec147d4e5720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5026daa1-5493-55d5-b06a-ec147d4e5720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572916} :answer-field/id #uuid "41834297-4e3f-5346-8eb0-62cb1520f127" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61cd2eda-8e2b-568d-83db-33ce3428cd1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-311278" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=2.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=2} & =3{q}^{′}(2)+4{r}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =3(-3)+4(2) \\\\  & =-9+8 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445164} :answer-field/id #uuid "72717550-a6aa-5a9b-8df2-1401d5e8c09c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "820989f9-6d7d-594e-a9c9-c00397b747b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-311283" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $t=3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $-2$ | $6$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2+h(t)}{z(t)},$ compute  ${f}^{′}(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2+h(t)$ and $v=z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}={h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{h}^{′}(t)z(t)-(2+h(t)){z}^{′}(t)}{{z}^{2}(t)}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=3,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =\\frac{{h}^{′}(3)z(3)-(2+h(3)){z}^{′}(3)}{{z}^{2}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 6-(2+(-2))(-1)}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-(0)(-1)}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290f52b2-20e6-5905-988c-748802b627d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "290f52b2-20e6-5905-988c-748802b627d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312286} :answer-field/id #uuid "c222c8e2-34bd-53c8-8877-54fd0121599e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9a67f2b8-f03c-57a0-a261-901981830dca" :question/math-academy-id "q-341468" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(t)$ and $z(t)$ and their derivatives at $t=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2h(t)-5}{1-z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(4).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2h(t)-5$ and $v=1-z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2{h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-{z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2{h}^{′}(t)(1-z(t))-(2h(t)-5)(-{z}^{′}(t))}{(1-z(t))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{2{h}^{′}(4)(1-z(4))-(2h(4)-5)(-{z}^{′}(4))}{(1-z(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(1-(-2))-(2(1)-5)(-1)}{(1-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(3)-(-3)(-1)}{(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18-3}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66bba579-8ea0-5e5c-bd2d-e8e863cdd735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572949} {:answer/id #uuid "824adea5-acf8-5e06-8bab-443fe02ee9b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572991} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3f00e8-0aa4-5703-a339-a7d82486ce71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573005} {:answer/id #uuid "bd51a5c9-fd39-575f-ac7e-0441c9c8a065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573064} {:answer/id #uuid "c469cea9-c5ed-510d-9d4e-23fad7086af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "824adea5-acf8-5e06-8bab-443fe02ee9b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572991} :answer-field/id #uuid "11c76a28-9fde-5aa9-9195-610b2d3249af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b93f5e4-441e-52cb-bcd1-657f8b3f7ca5" :question/math-academy-id "q-48724" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-2)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(-2)=-3,\\,g(-2)=2,\\,{g}^{′}(-2)=6\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-2} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(-2)g(-2)-f(-2){g}^{′}(-2)}{{g}^{2}(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 6}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341895 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158ef797-3c95-5bcd-9718-13a56de44516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339318} {:answer/id #uuid "367510c1-9a7d-5efc-9a23-2d2dab4e5e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339615} {:answer/id #uuid "4bce8f0b-d42b-5d9d-86f7-87536d507436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339810} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9b66b0-f49d-525c-93bf-5c48acfa8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340523} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e6fda6-a5b1-52d7-9e11-0a56fd7ca0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a9b66b0-f49d-525c-93bf-5c48acfa8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340523} :answer-field/id #uuid "02a49899-89cd-5419-a9ac-3c21bb420e9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bd63bec-2f2e-5dc7-9fc2-4882af93d878" :question/math-academy-id "q-72996" :question/problem "For the functions $e(x)$ and $n(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\ne(-5)=5,\\,{e}^{′}(-5)=-6,\\,n(-5)=-7,\\,{n}^{′}(-5)=9\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))$ at $x=-5.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))=3{e}^{′}(x)+{n}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))|}_{x=-5} & =3{e}^{′}(-5)+{n}^{′}(-5) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-6)+9 \\\\  & =-18+9 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d99022f-a106-59b1-ab19-2a49af098a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572960} {:answer/id #uuid "80d2e7ff-b678-5e91-8bb8-bd913d289e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572989} {:answer/id #uuid "d35a0e4c-6b8e-55dd-80ae-ee8bb4fd321a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573091} {:answer/id #uuid "dd954a77-5150-5c82-acfe-3e055cf99c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573106} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb7f59e-6f91-5b88-b360-42fd9db4647c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d35a0e4c-6b8e-55dd-80ae-ee8bb4fd321a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573091} :answer-field/id #uuid "79ae0370-2dd2-570e-83d6-5d0437db891c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26a28da3-48f6-5069-8f6b-b7cd82087ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-72999" :question/problem "For the functions $g(x)$ and $u(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\ng(-2)=-6,\\,{g}^{′}(-2)=3,\\,u(-2)=4,\\,{u}^{′}(-2)=-8\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2g(x)+u(x))$ at $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2g(x)+u(x))=2{g}^{′}(x)+{u}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2g(x)+u(x))|}_{x=-2} & =2{g}^{′}(-2)+{u}^{′}(-2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3+(-8) \\\\  & =6-8 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
